TI  - Zero-Shot Clinical Data Extraction from Pathology Reports Using Llama 3.1.
PG  - 1818-1819
LID - 10.3233/SHTI251230 [doi]
AB  - This study evaluates the performance of the Llama 3.1 model with 70 billion 
      parameters (70b) in extracting clinically significant information from free-text 
      pathology reports under zero-shot learning conditions. The model achieved a 
      remarkable accuracy of 98%, directly generating structured outputs in JSON format 
      without requiring annotated examples. These findings demonstrate the potential of 
      Llama 3.1 in automating data extraction from complex medical documents, 
      streamlining clinical workflows, and enhancing the precision of information 
      retrieval in healthcare settings.
