JID - 101756300
PMC - PMC12311501
OAB - Large, diverse, and automatically updated registries of biopsy-proven 
      glomerulonephritis are lacking in supporting data science research and clinical 
      trial enrollment. Kidney biopsy reports are often in the nonindexed text format, 
      and the pathologic diagnosis requires labor-intensive manual review and 
      abstraction. Natural language processing models allow for data extraction from 
      free text reports, minimizing the need to create registries manually. Using a 
      cohort of 2,666 patients with 3,042 native kidney biopsy reports in the Portable 
      Document Format, from June 2016 to December 2023, we developed an accurate and 
      scalable model to extract the primary biopsy diagnosis from free-text kidney 
      biopsy reports. This creates a useful tool to easily identify patients with rare 
      kidney diseases to facilitate epidemiologic studies and clinical trial 
      recruitment.
