JID - 9918250414506676
PMC - PMC11958830
OAB - Pathology departments produce many diagnostic reports as free text, which is hard 
      to analyze or use in research and computer projects. Converting this free text 
      into more standard organized information like test results or diagnoses, makes it 
      easier to use. This task often requires human experts and takes time. Large 
      language models (LLMs), which are advanced computer systems designed to 
      understand and generate human-like text, might simplify this process. Here, we 
      tested six LLMs, including freely available models and the commercial GPT-4 
      model, using 579 pathology reports in English and German. Our results show that 
      freely available models can perform as well as commercial, providing a cheaper 
      solution while avoiding privacy concerns. The shared dataset will support future 
      research in pathology data processing.
